# Dual-pass reviewer charter

Full contract: [docs/REVIEWER_CHARTER.md](../../docs/REVIEWER_CHARTER.md)

## After any code change

The orchestrator **must** spawn **cavecrew-reviewer** using the **Spawn prompt** block from [docs/REVIEWER_CHARTER.md](../../docs/REVIEWER_CHARTER.md). Do not skip review for "small" edits.

## Required passes

The reviewer runs **both** passes on every diff:

1. **Pass A — Karpathy / agentic** — assumptions, simplicity, surgical scope, goal-driven verification.
2. **Pass B — Mathematical logic** — invariants from BLUEPRINT and authority PDFs in `docs/references/` (filtration, event-time, no lookahead, walk-forward, etc.).

Both passes must complete before the orchestrator proceeds to **Verify** (pytest / CHI404 gates).

## Math violation citations

When Pass B flags a math or invariant violation, the reviewer **must cite** the source section:

- `BLUEPRINT.md` section, or
- Full PDF name + section/page under `docs/references/`: `chicago_cme_microstructure_mathematical_model.pdf`, `chicago_cme_microstructure_a_plus_developer_handoff.pdf`, `chicago_cme_a_plus_production_implementation_prompt.pdf`, `rithmic_trial_hftbacktest_pipeline_prompt.pdf`, `Ultimate_Quantitative_Finance_Researcher.pdf`, `ultra_low_latency_hft_vector_search_architecture.pdf`.

Findings without a citation are incomplete for Pass B.

## Output

One line per finding:
`path:line: <emoji> <severity>: [Pass A|Pass B] <problem>. <fix>.`

Block merge on any 🔴 from either pass until resolved or explicitly accepted by the user.
